<title>UK: BAA shares dip after first-half results.</title>
<headline>BAA shares dip after first-half results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BAA Plc eased in early trading Monday after first-half results from the British airports operator.</p>
<p>Pre-tax profits rose 3.4 percent to 304 million stg in the six months to September 30 compared with consensus analysts forecasts ranging from 303 to 320 million stg.</p>
<p>However, BAA said following a change to the structure of airport charges, income from that source had been reduced by 11 million stg in the first half but would be recoverable in the second half.</p>
</text>
